%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e5243d49411170e49a1bac6c9ca10949, type: 3}
  m_Name: Passage_Act2_TheRoad
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SundayLastBreath.Data.StoryPassageData
  passageId: Act2_TheRoad
  passageTitle: ACT2 THEROAD
  associatedRoomId: 
  backdropSprite: {fileID: 0}
  keepPreviousBackdrop: 0
  animatedBackdropFrames: []
  animationFPS: 8
  musicAction: 0
  backgroundMusicOrAmbience: {fileID: 0}
  musicVolume: 0.5
  entranceSFX: {fileID: 0}
  sfxVolume: 0.8
  speakerName: 
  storyText: "/* =======================================================================\r\n   SYSTEM INITIALIZATION\r\n======================================================================= */\r\n/* Clear the map when leaving the building */"
  narrativeBeats:
  - "/* 1. CLEAR PREVIOUS AUDIO & START THE RIOT */\r\n    if (typeof window.HallwayAmbience !== 'undefined') window.HallwayAmbience.stop();\r\n    setup.sound.stopAll(); \r\n    \r\n    /* Play inside car ambiance */\r\n    setup.sound.play(\"inside_car\", \"audio/bgm/insidecar.mp3\", true, 0.4);"
  - THE ESCAPE
  - "Your chest heaves against the seatbelt. Your knuckles are white on the steering wheel, and there is dark, drying blood on your jacket that you are trying very hard not to look at. \r\n                \r\n                    You let out a long, shuddering breath as the doors lock with a mechanical *thunk*. Your hands are shaking\u2014not from pain, but from the sheer, overwhelming realization that you actually made it out."
  - The locked doors and the running engine are the only things separating you from the nightmare outside. The horrors of the Ascott Residency are shrinking in the rearview mirror.
  - The city is a nightmare in the glass. Plumes of thick black smoke rise from the downtown grid. Sirens echo endlessly in the distance, overlapping into a chaotic, directionless wail.
  - "Inside the car, it is jarringly quiet. The dashboard clock glows a faint, digital blue. \r\n                \r\n                \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                            \r\n                            \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                                    THE ESCAPE"
  - "/* =================================================================\r\n                                   COMPANION: VANE IS PRESENT\r\n                                ================================================================= */\r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                            Vane is in the passenger seat. The adrenaline that carried him through the lobby and the parking lot is finally crashing. He rests his forehead against the cool glass of the window, his eyes closed."
  - He opens his eyes, staring blankly at the passing, burning ruins of the city. He lets out a dry, humorless laugh.
  - He takes a slow, shuddering breath, then turns to look at you. The fear is still there, but now there's a desperate need for direction.
  - He traces the frayed edge of his ruined designer jacket.
  - To keep your hands from shaking, you force your mind to focus on a single point. You need a destination. You need a reason to keep the car on the road.
  - "/* =================================================================\r\n                                   COMPANION: PLAYER IS ALONE\r\n                                ================================================================= */\r\n                                \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                    \r\n                                    \r\n                                    \r\n                                        \r\n                                            The silence in the car is heavy. The empty passenger seat feels like a glaring reminder of everyone who didn't make it out of the lobby."
  - "Survivor's guilt is a cold thing. It starts in your stomach and creeps up your throat. The sheer scale of the collapse is setting in. The military has barricaded the bridges. The hospitals are gone. The world you knew yesterday is dead. \r\n                                            \r\n                                            \r\n                                                \r\n                                                    \r\n                                                        \r\n                                                        \r\n                                                        \r\n                                                        \r\n                                                            To keep your hands from shaking, you force your mind to focus on a single point. You need a destination. You need a reason to keep the car on the road."
  - "WHO IS WAITING FOR YOU OUTSIDE THE CITY?\r\n            \r\n            \r\n            \r\n                \r\n                    \r\n                    /* WIFE / GIRLFRIEND */\r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                            \r\n                                What is her name?\r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                                    Presets: \r\n                                     | \r\n                                     |"
  - "/* HUSBAND / BOYFRIEND */\r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                            \r\n                                What is his name?\r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                                    Presets: \r\n                                     | \r\n                                     |"
  - "/* NON-BINARY PARTNER */\r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                            \r\n                                What is their name?\r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                                    Presets: \r\n                                     | \r\n                                     |"
  - /* PARENTS (Bypasses Name Entry) */
  - /* LONE WOLF (Bypasses Name Entry) */
  dialogueLines:
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: Vane
    side: 1
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bb691f92d5ba23e60c2959dde5ee2a01, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: I didn't think we were getting out of that lobby. I really didn't.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: Vane
    side: 1
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bb691f92d5ba23e60c2959dde5ee2a01, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: My entire life was sponsorships, unboxing videos, aesthetic lighting... None of that prepared me for bludgeoning someone's skull in with a Pelican camera case.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: Vane
    side: 1
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bb691f92d5ba23e60c2959dde5ee2a01, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: I don't have anywhere to go. My family and I... we haven't spoken since I moved to the city to do my own thing.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: Vane
    side: 1
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bb691f92d5ba23e60c2959dde5ee2a01, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: My entire world was on a screen, and the internet is dead. I was just running to run. Where are we going?
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  initialFloorItems: []
